{"ts":"2026-07-04T18:49:46.376Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-04T18:49:46.376Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Unknown-option errors suggest valid flags via did-you-mean; list-closed projection is compact by default; schema add-field is discoverable from pm schema help output."}],"before_hash":"74d145b302b64931f7e6e4517ea252b4eb04a4a41909348c3fc784879e58aed6","after_hash":"ad66e0ff4864b5e6e432ce3e4c472e7a2aae2cd71c58c1d2b812a5946c6f9878"}
{"ts":"2026-07-04T19:18:53.002Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Context\nFrom the 2026-07-02 audit (Lane A, pm-kes3): three agent-UX output paper-cuts, batched as one polish pass over the shared arg-parse/render layers:\n\n1. Unknown-option errors don't list valid flags or a nearest-match suggestion — agents pay an extra contracts round-trip. Reuse the OSA Damerau suggester (2026-05-28 agent-UX pass) at the flag level; include the command's valid flags in the structured error payload.\n2. pm list-closed defaults to the full projection — closed queries are triage scans; default to the compact projection (id/status/type/title/closed_at) with --full opt-out, consistent with list --format defaults.\n3. pm schema add-field's field-definition flags are buried in the shared option list — group them under a dedicated help section (help renderer already supports sections).\n\n## Definition of done\nUnknown-flag error carries suggested_flags in the structured payload + human did-you-mean; list-closed compact by default with spec; schema add-field help shows a grouped section; contracts:update run for any flag-surface change."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-04T19:18:53.002Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"ad66e0ff4864b5e6e432ce3e4c472e7a2aae2cd71c58c1d2b812a5946c6f9878","after_hash":"973e5d700958cf0aea9776068316010efed2a2977f03e182bcdcf3e8453fbdcb"}
{"ts":"2026-07-07T14:17:50.385Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Context\nFrom the 2026-07-02 review (Lane A, pm-kes3): three agent-UX output paper-cuts, batched as one polish pass over the shared arg-parse/render layers:\n\n1. Unknown-option errors don't list valid flags or a nearest-match suggestion — agents pay an extra contracts round-trip. Reuse the OSA Damerau suggester (2026-05-28 agent-UX pass) at the flag level; include the command's valid flags in the structured error payload.\n2. pm list-closed defaults to the full projection — closed queries are triage scans; default to the compact projection (id/status/type/title/closed_at) with --full opt-out, consistent with list --format defaults.\n3. pm schema add-field's field-definition flags are buried in the shared option list — group them under a dedicated help section (help renderer already supports sections).\n\n## Definition of done\nUnknown-flag error carries suggested_flags in the structured payload + human did-you-mean; list-closed compact by default with spec; schema add-field help shows a grouped section; contracts:update run for any flag-surface change."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-07T14:17:50.385Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"From 2026-07-02 review (Lane A, pm-kes3): (1) unknown-option errors do not list valid flags or a nearest-match suggestion, forcing an extra contracts round-trip (agents should never be blocked by wrong flags); (2) pm list-closed defaults to the full projection (verbose for agents; closed queries are usually triage scans); (3) pm schema add-field help is buried in the shared option list, hard to discover the field-definition flags."}],"before_hash":"973e5d700958cf0aea9776068316010efed2a2977f03e182bcdcf3e8453fbdcb","after_hash":"66cccbede8838f185edafc0318949591d81aa909f58097932cc29f93b2af7eef"}
{"ts":"2026-07-07T14:19:22.611Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-07T14:19:22.611Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-07T14:19:22.611Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Fresh first-hand repro 2026-07-07 for defect 1: pm update <id> --expected-result ... -m 'msg' fails exit 2 'Unknown option -m' with zero suggestions, even though (a) --message exists on update and (b) -m is the close alias for the same concept — the cross-command hint layer shipped in pm-8nyc does not cover single-char short flags. Same alias-parity class as closed pm-1lws (--expected/--actual). Scope: did-you-mean must include short-flag aliases and cross-command parity for -m/--message on update. Note the failure is invisible under output truncation (| tail) — a second reason the structured error payload matters."}]}],"before_hash":"66cccbede8838f185edafc0318949591d81aa909f58097932cc29f93b2af7eef","after_hash":"66131263f952e6e06badcbb38cd457354a2f1c09880557316086578beccdf706"}
{"ts":"2026-07-07T14:45:57.827Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-07T14:45:57.827Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"2026-07-07 verified defect in the shipped flag suggester, same fix locus: the unknown-option error's cross-command hint list is INCOMPLETE and therefore misleading. Repro: 'pm notes pm-vvib --format json' errors with '--format is a valid option on: config, list, list-all' — but get, search (and more) also accept --format (verified exit 0 same session). Wrong information is worse than none: an agent following the hint abandons valid commands. Fix: derive the valid-on list from the same contracts source used by completion/SCHEMA_CONTRACTS instead of a partial index; add a contract test asserting every command accepting --format appears in the hint."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-07T14:45:57.827Z"}],"before_hash":"66131263f952e6e06badcbb38cd457354a2f1c09880557316086578beccdf706","after_hash":"755a30f0fdec85467c964946c9fed7bdaa36f1af4475ffa58ed4c66cddf3998a"}
{"ts":"2026-07-15T19:27:29.553Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-15T19:27:29.552Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Observation 2026-07-15 (review pass #89): near-miss flag typos hit a \"Refusing to auto-correct option --statuss to --status. Retry with the canonical flag\" error — the CLI has already computed the unique intended flag with high confidence, then spends the certainty on a refusal, guaranteeing agents one wasted roundtrip. Disposition option for this item (or fold into pm-0z7n alias-shim policy): config-gated auto-accept for SINGLE-candidate high-confidence flag corrections (accept + prominent corrected-from warning in the envelope; default remains refuse for ambiguous or multi-candidate cases). The maintainer never-block-agents directive (recurring; re-stated 2026-07-15) is the motivation; countervailing explicitness policy should be dispositioned against it in one place rather than left implicit."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-15T19:27:29.553Z"}],"before_hash":"755a30f0fdec85467c964946c9fed7bdaa36f1af4475ffa58ed4c66cddf3998a","after_hash":"8193dc36ab9ff4df347c93dc3aa1a94ab39a018b61b5420347f81755c8cba567"}
{"ts":"2026-07-17T21:40:24.664Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-17T21:40:24.664Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"New evidence for the incomplete flag-hint list defect (2026-07-17): `pm graph audit --format json` exits 2 with hint \"--format is a valid option on: config, list, list-all\" — omitting search (--format json|toon) and deps (--format context). Same defect, new surface; suggester's flag-holder enumeration is stale/partial. pm graph itself uses --json (correct per convention); only the hint text is wrong."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-17T21:40:24.664Z"}],"before_hash":"8193dc36ab9ff4df347c93dc3aa1a94ab39a018b61b5420347f81755c8cba567","after_hash":"57a4f838dcb71bd892787b33d0dee1e4b277397e4bb8b5d7fa916615093cd0a6"}
